1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,655
You may have drunk seawater today

2
00:00:01,655 --> 00:00:02,984
without tasting any salt!

3
00:00:02,984 --> 00:00:03,426
How?

4
00:00:03,626 --> 00:00:06,080
Saudi Arabia leads the world in desalination

5
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,382
using two main methods

6
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,425
Method one: boil the seawater

7
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:11,048
Only the water evaporates

8
00:00:11,048 --> 00:00:12,346
the salt stays at the bottom

9
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:14,039
Cool the steam: fresh water!

10
00:00:14,239 --> 00:00:16,156
Method two: reverse osmosis

11
00:00:16,156 --> 00:00:17,760
Push seawater with huge pressure

12
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,487
against a membrane with tiny holes

13
00:00:19,487 --> 00:00:21,480
Water slips through, salt gets stuck

14
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,180
It's the most common method today

15
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:24,828
because it saves a lot of energy

16
00:00:25,028 --> 00:00:26,329
So the water in your glass

17
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:27,607
may once have been in the sea!
